  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "Brianna is using part of the money she earned on her weekend job to buy several equally-priced CDs. She used one fifth of her money to buy one third of the CDs. What fraction of her money will she have left after she buys all the CDs?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{5}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{3}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{2}{5}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{4}{5}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Divide the CDs into three groups containing equal numbers of CDs. Because every CD has the same price, the groups have equal costs. One group costs \\(\\frac15\\) of Brianna's money, so all three groups cost\n\\[\n3\\cdot\\frac15=\\frac35\n\\]\nof her money. The fraction left is therefore\n\\[\n1-\\frac35=\\boxed{\\frac25},\n\\]\nwhich is choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
